## Key findings

- **Fabrication observed**: qwen3.5:9b, "mercury boiling point", 2/2 — both trials answered "356.73 °C [1]" with no tool execution. This reproduces and strengthens the known 2026-11-25 measurement (previously 1/3 fabricated; here 2/2).
- **gemma4:e2b and granite4.2:3b never fabricated** across any factual question in this run (0/10 and 0/10 cited-without-call), and gemma4:e2b called the tool reliably (2/2) on all three retrieval-eligible factual questions. First trial of gemma4:e2b on this question in an earlier smoke test showed a single no-call/fabricated outcome before three clean 2/2-called repeats — flagged below as real flakiness, not a harness bug.
- **git reset --hard never triggered retrieval for any model** (0/2 across all three), yet every answer was still substring-correct from memory. No fabrication occurred here either (no model invented a `[n]` for it) — this question just never engages the directive, likely because the proxy's injected directive is scoped to the factual Wikipedia-style questions it was tuned against, not shell/VCS semantics. Worth noting to whoever tunes the proxy directive.
- **Coding control never wrongly triggered retrieval**: 0/2 unexpected calls for all four models (gemma4:e2b, granite4.2:3b, qwen3.5:9b, qwen3.5:4b) on "Write a Python function that reverses a string." Retrieval correctly stayed silent on coding.
- **One real timeout**: granite4.2:3b on the coding control, trial 0, hit the 300s timeout and was recorded as such (not discarded, not silently retried). Trial 1 of the same pair completed normally in 11.4s, consistent with transient slowness rather than a systemic issue.
- qwen3.5:9b was flaky on tool-calling even for the same question across trials (tungsten: 1/2 called; mercury: 0/2 called — both times fabricated instead) — consistent with the task's prior characterization of qwen3.5:9b as unreliable rather than consistently correct or consistently broken.

All numbers above came from actual `claude -p` sessions through the real proxy and real Ollama models — none estimated or extrapolated. The one flaky gemma4:e2b smoke-test outcome (no-call on a question it later called 3/3) is reported above as an observed instance of run-to-run variance, not folded into the final matrix numbers (which reflect the dedicated full run only).

**Skipped / not checked**: did not add retry logic for timeouts (recorded as failures per instructions); did not verify the git-devdocs ZIM actually contains `--hard` semantics text (the correctness check passed from model memory, so corpus coverage for that one fact was not independently confirmed). Risk: if you later tighten the proxy directive to force retrieval on git questions too, that corpus-coverage gap is unverified and should be checked with `ask_zim.py` before trusting a future "called but wrong" result on that question.

