s://www.srinidevops.com)\n[![R\u00e9sum\u00e9](https://img.shields.io/badge/\ud83d\udcc4_R\u00e9sum\u00e9_(PDF)-4A5D75?style=for-the-badge)](https://www.srinidevops.com/resume.pdf)\n[![LinkedIn](https://img.shields.io/badge/LinkedIn-0A66C2?style=for-the-badge&logo=linkedin&logoColor=white)](https://www.linkedin.com/in/srini-solution-architect/)\n[![Email](https://img.shields.io/badge/Email-6B5570?style=for-the-badge&logo=gmail&logoColor=white)](mailto:<redacted-email>)\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udc4b Fast facts for recruiters &amp; engineering leads\n\n- **Current role:** DevOps / Platform Systems Engineer @ Thomson Reuters\n- **Scope:** release, upgrade &amp; disaster-recovery automation for a multitenant Azure platform of 15+ microservices \u2014 GitHub Actions, Ansible, Datadog\n- **Experience:** 5 years across DevOps, cloud platforms, and systems engineering\n- **Work authorization:** US citizen \u00b7 OCI cardholder for India \u2014 no visa sponsorship required\n- **Location:** Bengaluru, India (IST / UTC+5:30) \u2014 open to remote &amp; hybrid globally, with daily US Eastern &amp; Pacific overlap\n- **Credentials:** 24 verified industry credentials (AWS, Azure, Red Hat / Ansible, Datadog)\n- **Education:** Madras Institute of Technology, Anna University\n- **Focus:** MCP &amp; AI developer tooling, GitOps, chaos engineering, cloud cost optimization\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 Flagship engineering showcase\n\n| Project | Stack | What it does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **[repo2graph](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/repo2graph)** \u00b7 [live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/repo2graph) | Python \u00b7 tree-sitter \u00b7 MCP | Gives coding agents trustworthy, **cited** answers about a codebase \u2014 a code graph plus an MCP server, no LLM required. Parses 17 languages; BM25 + optional dense retrieval with enforced token budgets. Listed on the MCP Registry. |\n| **[pennywright](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/pennywright)** \u00b7 [live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/agentic-app-loop) | JavaScript \u00b7 Claude Code \u00b7 Codex | The utility belt for coding agents: `/penny` routes any request to a 7-phase build loop, a 5-member council, or a bounded scout \u2014 with token discipline throughout. |\n| **[self-healing-deployment](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/self-healing-deployment)** \u00b7 [live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/self-healing-deployment) | Python \u00b7 Ansible \u00b7 Blue/Green | Deployment pipeline that health-checks every release and auto-rolls-back on failure, with chaos experiments wired in. |\n| **[multicloud-free-tier](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/multicloud-free-tier)** \u00b7 [live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/multi-cloud-free-tier-platform) | Python \u00b7 Terraform \u00b7 AWS/Azure/GCP/Oracle | One dashboard to provision and monitor real free-tier servers across four clouds. |\n| **[tokenmiser](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/tokenmiser)** \u00b7 [live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/tokenmiser) | JavaScript \u00b7 Claude Code | Instruction files, skills, and benchmarks that teach Claude Code to do the same work with fewer tokens \u2014 attacking re-sent context, not reply length. |\n| **[browser-pdf-tools](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/browser-pdf-tools)** \u00b7 [live](https://srinidevops.com/browser-pdf-tools/) | JavaScript \u00b7 Client-side | Merge, split, and rearrange PDFs entirely in the browser \u2014 files never leave the device. |\n\nAlso in the workshop: **[doc2md-action](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/doc2md-action)** ([live](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects/doc2md-action)) \u00b7\n**[filescan-hub](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/filescan-hub)** \u00b7\n**[minecraft-server-gitops](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/minecraft-server-gitops)** \u00b7\n**[authormark-watch](https://github.com/Srinivasan-78/authormark-watch)** \u2014\nor [explore all 23 builds](https://www.srinidevops.com/projects).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfe2 Enterprise track record\n\n**Thomson Reuters \u2014 DevOps &amp; Platform Systems Engineer**\n- Re-architected a multi-terabyte Azure Storage migration from a 48-hour weekend window to roughly 4 hours with **0% data loss**, using chunked delta detection and parallel AzCopy orchestration.\n- Replaced multi-page manual recovery runbooks with single-click self-service GitHub Actions workflows \u2014 **RTO under 5 minutes**, including automated Azure NLB regional cutovers.\n- Built a fail-fast synthetic validation gate that verifies service state, HTTP 200, load-balancer convergence, and the health-check file *before* live traffic is routed, with retry/backoff so a slow start is never mistaken for a failure.\n- Drove double-digit-percentage cloud storage cost savings through tiering and lifecycle automation.\n\n**Granite River Labs \u2014 Systems / DevOps Engineer**\n- Automated the Project MATTER / CSA and Zigbee smart-home compliance test-runner image pipeline, with hardware-in-the-loop rigs and automated packet-capture diagnostics on GitLab CI.\n- Cut compliance test-setup cycles by more than half.\n- Architected multi-architecture (Buildx) container pipelines with semantic versioning, vulnerability scanning, and multi-registry push orchestration.\n- Authored the Wireshark THREAD protocol Windows installer (WiX) \u2014 [merged upstream into Wireshark](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/11008).\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Technical skills\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n**\u2601\ufe0f Cloud platforms**\n\n![AWS](https://img.shields.io/badge/AWS-232F3E?style=for-the-badge&logo=amazonwebservices&logoColor=white)\n![Azure](https://img.shields.io/badge/Azure-0078D4?style=for-the-badge&logo=microsoftazure&logoColor=white)\n\n**\ud83d\udcd0 IaC &amp; automation**\n\n![Terraform](https://img.shields.io/badge/Terraform-7B42BC?style=for-the-badge&logo=terraform&logoColor=white)\n![Ansible](https://img.shields.io/badge/Ansible-EE0000?style=for-the-badge&logo=ansib