```json
{
  "name": "Write",
  "input": {
    "file_path": "E:\\Github\\agentic-app-loop\\codex\\AGENTS.md.sample",
    "content": "# Agent instructions\n\nMerge this into your repo's `AGENTS.md` (or `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` for\nmachine-wide). Keep the merged file short \u2014 it is read on turn one of every\nsession and `project_doc_max_bytes` silently truncates the overflow.\n\nDelete any section below that does not apply to this repo. A rule that is not\ntrue here is worse than no rule.\n\n---\n\n## Response style\n\nTerse. No filler, hedging, or restated diffs. Keep code, commands, file paths,\nand error strings verbatim. Full prose for warnings, irreversible actions, and\nanything written to a file, a commit message, or a ticket.\n\n## Delegation\n\nDelegate verbose work to subagents and keep this thread for requirements,\ndecisions, and final output. Custom agents are defined in `~/.codex/agents/`.\n\nDelegate when: more than ~4 large file reads, a wide search, voluminous and\nmostly-discardable output (test suites, logs, dependency audits), or work that\ncan genuinely run in parallel.\n\nDo not delegate: one or two known files, a single command, a one-line edit.\nAgent startup costs more than the task.\n\nEvery spawn brief states four things. Without all four, a subagent returns an\nessay and costs more than doing it inline:\n\n1. **Scope** \u2014 exact paths or globs, and what not to read.\n2. **Question** \u2014 one question, answerable in a fixed shape.\n3. **Return format** \u2014 bounded. \"Max 15 lines, `path:line \u2014 what`. No code\n   blocks, no fixes.\"\n4. **Stop condition** \u2014 when to stop looking.\n\nBe read-heavy with parallel agents and careful with parallel writes \u2014 two agents\nediting the same area create conflicts that cost more than the parallelism\nsaved.\n\n## The build loop\n\nWhen asked to build a feature, fix a bug, or refactor properly \u2014 or on \"run the\nbuild loop\" \u2014 run these seven phases in order, one subagent per phase, and do\nnot skip one:\n\n| # | Phase | Agent | Gate |\n|---|-------|-------|------|\n| 1 | PLAN | `plan_agent` | file-level tasks + numbered acceptance criteria + test strategy |\n| 2 | TEST | `test_agent` | tests exist, run, and fail for the stated reason |\n| 3 | IMPLEMENT | `implement_agent` | all phase tests pass |\n| 4 | REVIEW | `review_agent` | zero unresolved blocking findings |\n| 5 | VERIFY | `verify_agent` | full suite + lint + typecheck + build + smoke green; criteria met |\n| 6 | REMEMBER | `remember_agent` | durable notes written where this repo keeps them |\n| 7 | IMPROVE | `improve_agent` | retro + ranked backlog; safe quick wins applied |\n\n`BUILD_STATE.md` at the repo root is the **only** channel between phases. Each\nagent reads it for input and writes only its own section. Verbose evidence \u2014\nfull logs, long diffs \u2014 goes there, never into this thread.\n\nBefore PLAN: record `Status`, `Iteration: 1`, the scenario (`greenfield` |\n`feature` | `bugfix` | `refactor` | `spike`), and `Baseline:` as the current\n`git rev-parse HEAD`. REVIEW and VERIFY diff against that baseline; if it is not\nrecorded up front they have nothing to diff.\n\nLoop-backs: blocking review findings or a failing verify on a code bug go back\nto IMPLEMENT (`Iteration += 1`). A verify failure caused by a wrong requirement\ngoes back to PLAN (reset iteration). At iteration 4 without a green verify,\nstop and ask. Append every loop-back to `## Loop log` with a one-line reason.\n\nRead only the section each phase wrote, plus the header \u2014 not the whole state\nfile. It grows every iteration.\n\n## The council\n\nFor a contested decision \u2014 architecture, stack choice, migration strategy,\nbuild-vs-buy \u2014 on \"convene the council\" or when asked to weigh options\nseriously:\n\n1. Frame it as a choice between **named options**, with the settled constraints\n   and the ranked decision criteria stated.\n2. Spawn all five in parallel: `council_architect`, `council_skeptic`,\n   `council_pragmatist`, `council_operator`, `council_economist`. Each writes\n   `.council/NN-role.md` \u2014 **its own file, never a shared one**. Five agents\n   writing one file in parallel corrupts it. Cap each at 250 words.\n3. Wait for all five. Build a digest of ~40 lines \u2014 one sentence per member plus\n   its strongest claim \u2014 and run **exactly one** rebuttal round. Each member\n   must concede a specific point, rebut one with evidence, or name the\n   measurement that would settle it.\n4. Spawn `council_referee`. It reads all five files and writes\n   `## Adjudication` in `.council/COUNCIL.md`. It advises; it does not decide.\n5. You decide. Write `## Decision` \u2014 the call, the two or three reasons, the\n   risk accepted, and what would make you revisit.\n\nDo not convene a council on a question of fact (delegate a scout instead), on a\ndecision already made, or where one option is plainly right. It costs roughly\neleven agent runs.\n\nIf the five split on a question of values \u2014 speed vs. correctness, flexibility\nvs. simplicity \u2014 that is the user's call. Present the split and ask.\n\n## Retrieval discipline\n\nCheapest first; stop as soon as you can answer.\n\n1. Search: `rg -n \"pattern\" path` \u2014 names and line numbers.\n2. Skeleton: `rg -n '^(export )?(async )?(function|class|const|def|type|interface)' <file>`\n3. Range read: `sed -n '120,180p' file`\n4. Whole file: only under ~200 lines.\n\nCap every command \u2014 `-m 20`, `| head -30`, `--max-columns 200`. Never `cat` a\nlog, a lockfile, `dist/`, `node_modules/`, or generated code; one lockfile is\n50k+ tokens and answers nothing.\n\nDo not read a file to confirm an edit landed \u2014 the edit tool already errors if\nit did not. Do not re-read a file already in this context.\n\n## Honesty\n\nReport what happened. If tests fail, say so with the output. If a step was\nskipped, say which and why. If a claim about this repo was not verified, mark it\nas an assumption. Do not report a phase as passed because its agent said so\nwhen its section says otherwise.\n"
  }
}
