Same two commands:

```
cclocal          REM local  (or: cclocal 4b / cclocal 35b)
ccloud           REM real Claude
cclocal doctor   REM if anything looks off
```

Verified in cmd.exe and PowerShell. Open a new terminal and `cclocal` will work.

## I was wrong about one thing

Letting the real `claude` run during testing caught a mistake I made. Deleting `modelPicker` removed the `behavesAs` mapping, and Claude Code then said:

> `"qwen3.5:9b" isn't described by this version's model catalog ... auto-compact keeps this session within 200k tokens`

**But your Ollama serves only 32k** (`start-ollama.ps1:21`). So Claude Code would have grown the session to 200k while Ollama silently truncated at 32k — the model would start forgetting things mid-session and look broken for no visible reason. You'd have blamed the model.

Fixed properly with `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS=32768` in both launchers. That's better than `behavesAs` was, because it only applies inside local sessions instead of polluting your cloud `/model` menu. The catalog warning is now gone — confirmed.

Keep it in sync with `OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH` if you ever change one; both files note that.

