## The real bug — and I owe you an apology

Your `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` had a **`/v1` suffix**. Claude Code appends `/v1/messages` itself, so every request went to `/v1/v1/messages`:

```
/v1/messages     -> HTTP 200
/v1/v1/messages  -> HTTP 404   <- what your scripts produced
```

A 404 surfaces as *"model may not exist or you may not have access to it"* — which is why it looked like a model problem for this entire session. It was in your original scripts from the start, and I kept chasing env-var and PATH symptoms instead of checking the actual request path. I should have run one live prompt at the very beginning rather than testing `curl` against a URL I'd constructed by hand.

I was also wrong to delete `modelPicker` — it's load-bearing. Without a `behavesAs` row, Claude Code rejects unknown ids with `unrecognized_model`. It's restored, and in **global** settings, which the schema confirms is required (`modelPicker` is "not honored from a project checkout" — so it never would have worked where you originally had it).

