## Top 5 (really top 3 + 2 strong positives)

1. **COMPAT-01** — `doctor`'s Python-version check is broken for real-world use via a tuple-length comparison bug; it will misfire for nearly every 3.13 installation, undermining the one tool meant to build user trust during onboarding. Trivial one-line fix (`vi[:2]`).
2. **COMPAT-02** — genuine 3.10-era dead code/doc residue in 3 files, exactly the pattern the brief predicted, confirmed by grep.
3. **CFG-01** — three env vars undocumented, one of them (`REPO2GRAPH_ALLOW_INSECURE_OLLAMA`) is a security-relevant bypass users can only discover by tripping the error it suppresses.
