s the honest fix. The API offers no `fixed` dismissal reason (only\n`fix_started`, `inaccurate`, `no_bandwidth`, `not_used`, `tolerable_risk`), and a dismissal does\n**not** reopen if a later lock change reintroduces a vulnerable version \u2014 so dismissing a\ngenuinely-fixed alert permanently blinds you to that regression.\n\nRelated: [[solo-account-merge-gates]], [[tree-sitter-cap-is-a-security-boundary]].\n"
