  "input": {
    "file_path": "C:\\Users\\Srini\\obs-staging\\AUDIO_WEBCAM_AUDIT.md",
    "content": "# Audio & Webcam Audit + Target Spec\nScope: `C:\\Users\\Srini\\AppData\\Roaming\\obs-studio\\basic\\scenes\\Main.json`, all 4 profiles' `basic.ini`, and the newest OBS logs. Read-only audit \u2014 no OBS config files were modified. Live hardware enumerated via PowerShell `Get-PnpDevice`/`Get-CimInstance` and `ffmpeg -f dshow -list_options`.\n\nLegend: **OBSERVED** = read directly from a file/log/live enumeration. **INFERRED** = my judgment/recommendation, not a direct observation. Every inferred item is labeled.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Real hardware (OBSERVED, `Get-CimInstance`/`Get-PnpDevice`, all Status=OK)\n\n| Device | Class | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Brio 100** | Camera | Logitech USB webcam, `VID_046D&PID_094C` |\n| **Microphone (Brio 100)** | AudioEndpoint | Mic capsule built into the Brio 100 |\n| **Speakers (High Definition Audio Device)** | AudioEndpoint | Generic HD Audio render endpoint (motherboard/onboard codec render path \u2014 exact physical jack not determinable from PnP alone) |\n| NVIDIA High Definition Audio | Media | GPU HDMI/DP audio render device (`VEN_10DE`) |\n| High Definition Audio Device | Media | Realtek onboard codec (`VEN_10EC`, dev 0897) |\n| NVIDIA Broadcast | Media | NVIDIA's virtual-cam/mic software layer (root virtual device) |\n| Brio 100 (second MEDIA entry) | Media | The camera's audio-capable interface node (MI_02) |\n\nNo other microphones, headsets, or capture cards are present on this machine. **The only microphone in the system is the one built into the Brio 100 webcam.** There is no dedicated XLR/USB streaming mic.\n\n### Confirmed by OBS log (`2026-10-31 01-34-10.txt`)\n```\nWASAPI: Device 'Speakers (High Definition Audio Device)' [48000 Hz] initialized (source: Desktop Audio)\nWASAPI: Device 'Microphone (Brio 100)' [48000 Hz] initialized (source: Mic/Aux)\n[DShow Device: 'CAM - Webcam'] video device: Brio 100, resolution: 1920x1080, fps: 30.00, format: NV12\n[NVIDIA Audio Effects:] version: 1.6.1.2 \u2014 enabled\nnv-filters.dll loaded\n```\nBoth the mic and the system default playback device are running at 48000 Hz, matching `SampleRate=48000` in every profile \u2014 **no resample mismatch**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Webcam capability discovery\n\n**OBSERVED** (`ffmpeg -f dshow -list_options true -i video=\"Brio 100\"`):\n```\npixel_format=yuyv422  min s=1920x1080 fps=30 max s=1920x1080 fps=30\npixel_format=nv12     min s=1920x1080 fps=30 max s=1920x1080 fps=30\n```\nOnly a single mode is exposed through the DirectShow enumeration path on this machine: **1920x1080 @ 30 fps**, in YUY2 or NV12 (no MJPEG mode is offered at all). OBS is currently negotiating `video_format=0` (\"Any\") and the driver is handing it NV12 at 1080p30 \u2014 i.e., **OBS is already running at the only mode DirectShow reports for this device.**\n\n**INFERRED / caveat:** Windows' Frame Server bridge (MF\u2192DirectShow) frequently collapses a UVC camera's advertised mode list down to only the last-negotiated format when another app (or the previous session) already opened the camera \u2014 so lower resolutions (640x480, 1280x720) that the hardware likely also supports may simply not be surfacing here. I did not verify this with a cold-boot/registry check. Separately, by **published Logitech spec** (not verified live): the Brio 100 is Logitech's entry-level model and tops out at **1080p/30fps** \u2014 unlike the Brio 4K/Brio 500, it has no 720p60 or 1080p60 tier. If that spec is accurate, **the current 1920x1080@30 NV12 setting is already at this camera's ceiling** \u2014 there is no FPS or quality being left on the table by the current config, and MJPEG-vs-YUY2 CPU tradeoff doesn't apply here since this device apparently has no MJPEG mode to begin with (no onboard JPEG encoder on this budget model).\n\n**Bottom line:** current webcam settings (1080p30, NV12) = capable settings. No change recommended on resolution/FPS. If higher FPS is wanted, the only lever available is dropping to a lower resolution \u2014 recommend testing 1280x720@30 is also likely the only other tier.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Audio source audit (every `wasapi_input_capture` / `wasapi_output_capture` / `wasapi_process_output_capture` / `dshow_input`)\n\nAll settings below are OBSERVED directly from `Main.json`.\n\n### Desktop Audio (global, `wasapi_output_capture`)\n- Device: `default` \u2192 resolves to \"Speakers (High Definition Audio Device)\"\n- Filters (1): `Limiter` (`limiter_filter`) \u2014 threshold -2.0 dB, release 60 ms\n- Mixers: `192` (decoded: **no tracks 1\u20136 assigned** \u2014 see \u00a75)\n\n### Mic/Aux (global, `wasapi_input_capture`)\n- Device: `default` \u2192 resolves to \"Microphone (Brio 100)\"\n- Filters (5, in order):\n  1. Noise Suppression (`noise_suppress_filter`, versioned `noise_suppress_filter_v2`) \u2014 method `nvafx`, intensity 1.0\n  2. Noise Gate (`noise_gate_filter`) \u2014 open -35 dB, close -45 dB, attack 25 ms, hold 200 ms, release 150 ms\n  3. EQ (`basic_eq_filter`) \u2014 low -4.0, mid +0.5, high +3.0\n  4. Compressor (`compressor_filter`) \u2014 ratio 3:1, threshold -18 dB, attack 6 ms, release 60 ms, makeup +3.0 dB\n  5. Limiter (`limiter_filter`) \u2014 threshold -3.0 dB, release 60 ms\n- Mixers: `203` (decoded: tracks **1, 2, 4**)\n\n### CAM - Webcam (`dshow_input`)\n- Device: Brio 100, 1920x1080, 30fps (interval 333333), `video_format=0` (Any), `audio_output_mode=0` (audio disabled on this source \u2014 correct, mic is captured separately via Mic/Aux)\n- Filters (2): `Crisp` (`sharpness_filter`, 0.1), `Colour` (`color_filter`: gamma -0.04, contrast +0.08, saturation +0.22)\n- Mixers: `0` (no audio tracks \u2014 expected since `audio_output_mode=0`)\n\n### AUD - Game (`wasapi_process_output_capture`)\n- Target: `::VALORANT-Win64-Shipping.exe`\n- Filters: none\n- Mixers: `199` (decoded: tracks **1, 2, 3**)\n\n### AUD - Discord (`wasapi_process_output_capture`)\n- Target: `::Discord.exe`\n- Filters: none\n- Mixers: `211` (decoded: tracks **1, 2, 5**)\n- *(Per task instructions: Discord capture itself is authorized and not flagged as a privacy issue. Only its mix placement is audited \u2014 see \u00a75/\u00a76.)*\n\n### AUD - Music (Spotify) (`wasapi_process_output_capture`)\n- Target: `::Spotify.exe`\n- Filters (1): `Duck Under Mic` (`compressor_filter`) \u2014 ratio 8:1, threshold -32 dB, attack 15 ms, release 350 ms, sidechain source = Mic/Aux\n- Mixers: `225` (decoded: tracks **1, 6**)\n\n### AUD - Music (Browser) (`wasapi_process_output_capture`)\n- Target: `::firefox.exe`\n- Filters (1): identical `Duck Under Mic` ducking off Mic/Aux\n- Mixers: `225` (decoded: tracks **1, 6**)\n\n### Startup behavior (OBSERVED, consistent across all 2026-10-31 logs)\n`AUD - Game`, `AUD - Discord`, `AUD - Music (Spotify)`, and sometimes `AUD - Music (Browser)` log:\n```\n[WASAPISource::TryInitialize]:[[VIRTUAL_AUDIO_DEVICE_PROCESS_LOOPBACK]] Failed to find window\nWASAPI: Device '' failed to start (source: AUD - Game)\n```\nThis happens whenever the target .exe isn't running yet at OBS launch; OBS retries and the source self-heals once the process appears (seen succeeding later in several logs, e.g. `00-22-03.txt`: `WASAPI: Device '[VIRTUAL_AUDIO_DEVICE_PROCESS_LOOPBACK]' [48000 Hz] initialized`). **This is expected WASAPI process-loopback behavior, not a misconfiguration** \u2014 flagged only as a known startup-order cosmetic log entry, not a defect.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Webcam-adjacent filter chains\n\n### CAM - Webcam (`dshow_input`) \u2014 see \u00a73 above.\n\n### CAM - Card (`browser_source`)\n- `http://127.0.0.1:4466/cam-bg.html?...` \u2014 no filters.\n\n### CAM - Ambient Glow (`source-clone`, clones CAM - Webcam, audio cloning disabled)\n1. `Ambient Downscale` (`scale_filter`) \u2014 bilinear, 24x14\n2. `Ambient Blur` (`nv_blur_filter`) \u2014 strength 1.0 (NVIDIA GPU blur, confirms `nv-filters.dll` is also providing video effects, not just audio)\n3. `Ambient Tone` (`color_filter`) \u2014 contrast -0.25, brightness -0.3, saturation +0.6, opacity 0.45\n\n### CAM - Frame (`browser_source`)\n- No OBS filters, but **OBSERVED defect**: the log shows this browser source throwing JS errors every load:\n```\n[obs-browser: 'CAM - Frame'] Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'appendChild')\n[obs-browser: 'CAM - Frame'] Uncaught SyntaxError: Identifier 'obsCSS' has already been declared\n```\nThis points to the `reactive.html?mode=frame` page being loaded/injected twice (classic obs-browser double-init bug \u2014 `restart_when_active: true` combined with a scene re-entry re-running a script that isn't idempotent). Outside pure audio/webcam filter scope but noted since it was caught during this audit.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Audio routing table \u2014 mixer bitmask decode and track layout\n\nOBS's `mixers` field is a bitmask where bit *i* (0-indexed) = Track *i+1*, for tracks 1\u20136 (`MAX_AUDIO_MIXES = 6`; bits above bit 5 do nothing in OBS core).\n\n**OBSERVED anomaly:** every single audio source's `mixers` value carries bits 6 and 7 set as well (adds 192 to every value: Desktop Audio=192, Mic/Aux=203, Game=199, Discord=211, Spotify/Browser=225, HUD-Mic Muted=255). These bits are outside OBS's valid 6-track range and are currently harmless no-ops \u2014 but they indicate whatever tool wrote these bitmasks (almost certainly a prior `SetInputAudioMixers` obs-websocket call) miscalculated the mask. **INFERRED \u2014 flagged for cleanup so future scripted edits don't inherit the same off-by-bits mistake.**\n\nDecoding only the valid low 6 bits:\n\n| Source | mixers (raw) | Track 1 (Stream) | Track 2 (VOD-safe) | Track 3 | Track 4 | Track 5 | Track 6 | Monitoring |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Desktop Audio | 192 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | None |\n| Mic/Aux | 203 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2014 | None |\n| AUD - Game | 199 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | None |\n| AUD - Discord | 211 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2714 | \u2014 | None |\n| AUD - Music (Spotify) | 225 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2714 | None |\n| AUD - Music (Browser) | 225 | \u2714 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2714 | None |\n| CAM - Webcam (dshow audio) | 0 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | None (audio disabled on source) |\n| HUD - Mic Muted (browser) | 255 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2714 | \u2714 | None (`reroute_audio: false`, currently inert) |\n\n**All monitoring_type values are 0 (None)** across every source. There is zero OBS-internal monitoring configured, so there is **no echo/double-audio risk from OBS monitoring settings today** \u2014 the streamer must be relying on hardware/driver-level headphone monitoring outside OBS.\n\n### Profile cross-reference (OBSERVED, `basic.ini`)\n\n| Profile | RecTracks | TrackIndex (stream) | VodTrackIndex | VodTrackEnabled |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Stream and Record | **61** = tracks 1,3,4,5,6 | 1 | 2 | true |\n| Archive - High Quality | **1** = track 1 only | 1 | 2 | (not set in this profile) |\n| Fallback - Lightweight | 1 | 1 | 2 | (not set) |\n| Stream Only - No Record | 1 | 1 | 2 | (not set) |\n\n### Does per-source isolation actually work?\n\n**Track 1** = full live stream mix (Mic + Game + Discord + Music) \u2014 correct, everyone intended to be heard live is on it.\n\n**Track 2** = Mic + Game + Discord, **excluding both music sources**. Combined with `VodTrackIndex=2` + `VodTrackEnabled=true` (Twitch's native \"VOD Track\" feature, which muxes a second audio track into the RTMP stream specifically so Twitch can swap in a music-free mix for the archived VOD, avoiding copyright claims on recorded VODs) \u2014 **this is correctly built, not a bug.** It is a deliberate, well-executed DMCA-safe-VOD track. It only works, however, in the \"Stream and Record\" profile, and only if the configured streaming service actually honors the Twitch VOD Track option.\n\n**Tracks 3/4/5/6** = clean per-source solo isolation (Game / Mic / Discord / Music respectively) \u2014 all isolate correctly, one source each (Music sharing track 6 between Spotify and Browser is fine since in practice only one plays at a time).\n\n**So: yes, isolated per-source recording tracks work correctly \u2014 but only on the \"Stream and Record\" profile.** `RecTracks=61` there correctly includes tracks 1,3,4,5,6 (track 2 is intentionally excluded from the *local* recording because it's delivered to Twitch via the stream, not meant to be a second local file).\n\n**Defect:** \"**Archive - High Quality**\" \u2014 the profile whose entire purpose is a high-fidelity archival recording (AV1, hybrid MP4) \u2014 has `RecTracks=1`, i.e. it only ever writes the single flattened live mix. All the per-source isolation work (clean mic-only, clean game-only, clean Discord-only, clean music-only tracks) is **silently unavailable** in the one profile most likely to be used for post-production/editing. This defeats the purpose of the whole multi-track audio architecture whenever this profile is active.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Defects, ranked by severity\n\n1. **(HIGH) `AUD - Game` is hardcoded to Valorant and is reused, unchanged, in every non-Valorant scene.** `AUD - Game`'s `window` setting is `::VALORANT-Win64-Shipping.exe`, but the same single source is placed into scene `2 - Minecraft` (which uses `CAP - Minecraft` for video) and is the only game-audio source defined at all (no equivalent exists for \"CAP - The Finals\" / \"CAP - Any Game\"). When streaming anything other than Valorant, this source will never find its target process and game audio will be silent on every track that includes it (1, 2, 3). This is OBSERVED directly from the scene-item lists and the source settings, and explains the recurring \"Failed to find window\" log lines outside of simple startup-race timing.\n2. **(HIGH) \"Archive - High Quality\" profile loses all multi-track isolation** (`RecTracks=1`) despite the collection being built specifically for per-source isolated tracks. See \u00a75.\n3. **(MEDIUM) No de-esser anywhere in the mic chain.** The mic chain ends Noise Suppression \u2192 Gate \u2192 EQ (+3 dB high boost) \u2192 Compressor \u2192 Limiter. Boosting highs on a small condenser capsule like the Brio 100's and then compressing increases perceived sibilance, and nothing in the chain controls it. OBS ships no native de-esser filter, so this requires a VST plugin \u2014 see Target Spec. **INFERRED severity** (I have not heard the actual voice; this is a structural gap, not a measured problem).\n4. **(MEDIUM) Mic/Aux and Desktop Audio are both pinned to `device_id: \"default\"` rather than the specific device.** If the Windows default recording/playback device ever changes (OS update, a device being plugged in, auto-switching to HDMI), these sources silently follow the new default rather than staying locked to \"Microphone (Brio 100)\" / the intended speakers. Low likelihood, but it is a silent-failure mode with no OBS-side warning.\n5. **(LOW, cosmetic) Desktop Audio source is fully active (not muted) but assigned to zero tracks (1\u20136).** It still runs its own Limiter filter for no functional purpose. This is actually the *correct* defensive choice (it prevents Desktop Audio from duplicating audio that's already captured per-process via AUD-Game/Discord/Spotify/Browser, and it means **no Windows notification/system sound leak risk exists today** since Desktop Audio touches no track) \u2014 but it's dead weight that should either be muted or removed for clarity.\n6. **(LOW, cosmetic/latent) All `mixers` bitmasks carry stray bits 6 and 7 (+192) outside OBS's valid 6-track range.** Harmless under the current 6-track limit, but indicates a scripted/websocket edit miscalculated its bitmask; worth cleaning before further scripted changes compound the mistake. `HUD - Mic Muted` additionally has `mixers=255` (all 8 bits) while `reroute_audio: false` \u2014 currently inert, but a trap if `reroute_audio` is ever toggled on for troubleshooting, since it would instantly dump that HUD browser source's own audio into every track including the live stream mix and the VOD-safe track.\n7. **(LOW) Compressor attack time on Mic/Aux (6 ms) is fast enough to risk audibly \"pumping\" on hard consonants/plosives** given the Noise Gate's own fast 25 ms attack right before it. **INFERRED**, not measured \u2014 flagged as a tuning candidate only.\n8. **(INFO, not a defect) Discord routing.** Per the task's authorization, Discord capture itself is not flagged. Its mix placement (tracks 1, 2, 5) is correct: present in the live stream mix, present in the music-free VOD-safe mix, and isolated solo on track 5. No wrong-mix issue found for Discord.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Target spec (concrete values, for programmatic application via obs-websocket)\n\n### 7.1 Mic chain \u2014 `Mic/Aux` (device: Microphone (Brio 100))\n\nApply via `SetSourceFilterSettings` on each existing filter / `CreateSourceFilter` for the new one. Order matters \u2014 this is the desired top-to-bottom order:\n\n| # | Filter name | OBS filter id | Settings |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Noise Suppression | `noise_suppress_filter_v2` | `{\"method\": \"nvafx\", \"intensity\": 0.9}` \u2014 drop from 1.0 to 0.9 to reduce nvafx over-processing artifacts on a capsule this small; nvafx is correctly chosen over RNNoise/Speex given NVIDIA Broadcast/nv-filters is confirmed installed and running (log: `[NVIDIA Audio Effects:] enabled`, v1.6.1.2). |\n| 2 | Noise Gate | `noise_gate_filter` | `{\"open_threshold\": -34.0, \"close_threshold\": -42.0, \"attack_time\": 15, \"hold_time\": 150, \"release_time\": 100}` \u2014 integrated webcam capsules run a higher noise floor than a dedicated mic; this keeps normal speech open while still closing on room noise. **INFERRED values**, not measured against this specific room \u2014 verify against an actual noise-floor reading before finalizing. |\n| 3 | EQ | `basic_eq_filter` | `{\"low\": -5.0, \"mid\": 0.0, \"high\": 4.0}` \u2014 slightly deeper low cut (rumble/handling noise) and a touch more high presence than current, since Brio-class capsules read thin/boxy; zeroing the mid removes the current +0.5 bump which does nothing audible. |\n| 4 | Compressor | `compressor_filter` | `{\"ratio\": 3.0, \"threshold\": -18.0, \"attack_time\": 10, \"release_time\": 80, \"output_gain\": 4.0}` \u2014 attack slowed from 6\u219210 ms to reduce pumping risk right after the fast noise gate; release lengthened slightly for smoother gain recovery. |\n| 5 | De-esser | `vst_filter` | No native OBS de-esser exists. Load a free de-esser/dynamic-EQ VST (e.g. TDR Nova in de-ess mode) via `vst_filter` with settings `{\"plugin_path\": \"<path to .dll>\", \"chunk_data\": \"<plugin-specific>\"}`. Target band ~5\u20138 kHz, threshold \u2248 -24 dB, fast release. **This entire item is INFERRED/recommended \u2014 no VST is currently installed; I did not verify any specific plugin is present on this machine.** If a VST is not wanted, the pragmatic fallback is to retune filter #3's high band down 1\u20132 dB after listening tests rather than true de-essing. |\n| 6 | Limiter | `limiter_filter` | `{\"threshold\": -3.0, \"release_time\": 60}` \u2014 unchanged, already correctly placed last as the hard safety ceiling. |\n\n### 7.2 Webcam \u2014 `CAM - Webcam` (dshow_input)\n\n- Keep: `{\"video_device_id\": \"Brio 100:...\", \"resolution\": \"1920x1080\", \"frame_interval\": 333333, \"res_type\": 1, \"video_format\": 0, \"audio_output_mode\": 0}` \u2014 this is already the hardware's ceiling (\u00a72); no change.\n- Filters: keep `Crisp` (`sharpness_filter`, `{\"sharpness\": 0.1}`) and `Colour` (`color_filter`) but bump brightness slightly: `{\"gamma\": -0.04, \"contrast\": 0.08, \"brightness\": 0.03, \"saturation\": 0.22, \"hue_shift\": 0.0}` \u2014 a small lift to compensate for this camera's typically dim auto-exposure under non-studio lighting. **INFERRED**, cosmetic preference, verify visually.\n\n### 7.3 Track layout (formalize what's already working, fix what isn't)\n\n| Track | Purpose | Sources |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Live stream mix | Mic/Aux, AUD-Game*, AUD-Discord, AUD-Music(Spotify), AUD-Music(Browser) |\n| 2 | Twitch VOD-safe mix (no music) | Mic/Aux, AUD-Game*, AUD-Discord |\n| 3 | Game solo | AUD-Game* |\n| 4 | Mic solo | Mic/Aux |\n| 5 | Discord solo | AUD-Discord |\n| 6 | Music solo | AUD-Music(Spotify), AUD-Music(Browser) |\n\n*\\*Fix AUD-Game's process target per scene.* Recommend driving `AUD - Game`'s `window` setting from a scene-switch hook via `SetInputSettings`:\n```\n{\"inputName\": \"AUD - Game\", \"inputSettings\": {\"window\": \"::VALORANT-Win64-Shipping.exe\"}, \"overlay\": true}  // scene \"1 - Gaming\"\n{\"inputName\": \"AUD - Game\", \"inputSettings\": {\"window\": \"::javaw.exe\"}, \"overlay\": true}                     // scene \"2 - Minecraft\" \u2014 verify actual Minecraft process name/edition\n```\nfired on `CurrentProgramSceneChanged`. **INFERRED exact process name for Minecraft** \u2014 verify the real `.exe` name (Java edition is typically `javaw.exe`, Bedrock is `Minecraft.Windows.exe`) before wiring this up.\n\nProfile fix: set `RecTracks=63` (all 6 tracks, bits 0-5) in **Archive - High Quality**'s `[AdvOut]` section so archival recordings retain full per-source isolation. Leave Fallback/Stream-Only at `RecTracks=1` (intentional, by name).\n\nBitmask fix (via `SetInputAudioMixers`, recomputing cleanly without the stray +192):\n```\nDesktop Audio:        0   (unchanged \u2014 intentionally off every track)\nMic/Aux:              11  (tracks 1,2,4)\nAUD - Game:            7  (tracks 1,2,3)\nAUD - Discord:        19  (tracks 1,2,5)\nAUD - Music(Spotify): 33  (tracks 1,6)\nAUD - Music(Browser): 33  (tracks 1,6)\nHUD - Mic Muted:       0  (currently inert via reroute_audio:false; zero its mixers too so toggling reroute_audio can never leak it onto every track)\n```\n\n### 7.4 Monitoring\n