et token (C2) \u2014 both are plaintext, both are duplicated into backups, and the StreamElements one is additionally embedded in a browser-source URL that shows up in the Source Properties dialog.\n- **Fix in code:** the HUD server's unauthenticated `/ws.json` (H1), the unescaped `color` tag in chatbox.html (M1) \u2014 both are small, low-risk-of-exploitation but trivial-to-fix gaps.\n- **Confirmed safe / good pattern already in place:** HUD server is loopback-only by explicit code (not a judgment call \u2014 hardcoded `127.0.0.1` bind), chat message bodies and names are properly escaped, obs-meter.js's password-via-local-endpoint design is the right template to extend to the YouTube key (M2) and to StreamElements-style widgets (C2) going forward.\n- **Definitively LAN-exposed, not loopback:** obs-websocket (port 4456) \u2014 confirmed from its own startup log, not an assumption. This is inherent to the plugin (no bind-address setting exists), so the mitigation is password hygiene + a firewall rule, not a config change to obs-websocket itself.\n"
  }
}
