Taking "perf" as performance first, since I introduced the risk — then ideas.

Verified answer on perf: only **one** NVENC instance (`advanced_video_recording`) was created and the replay buffer started on top of it — so in Advanced mode **the replay buffer reuses the recording encoder rather than opening a second session**. Live you'll run **two** encode sessions total (H.264 stream + HEVC record/replay), well inside Ada's limit of eight. No dropped or skipped frames logged across any test run.

The real load isn't the encoder — it's the five browser sources plus a 1080p30 Brio plus the game. Watch **View → Stats** on your first The Finals session specifically; destruction physics is CPU-heavy and that's where contention shows up, not in Valorant.

