**Mouse redrawn** — the old version had the wheel overlapping both buttons, so a lit button bled into the middle. Now there's a clear channel between LMB and RMB, a divider line, the wheel drawn last so a lit button never covers it, and side buttons drawn *under* the shell so they read as inset into the flank.

## Element order

Everything now sits on one grid — a bottom-right block, right-anchored:

| | |
|---|---|
| **Row 1** | Data strip — score, map, mode, rank, today, uptime |
| **Row 2** | Input deck ◀ 20px gap ▶ Handcam |

Input deck and handcam share **identical top and bottom edges**; the strip sits directly above on the **same left edge**. Nothing touches Valorant's minimap, killfeed, abilities or ammo. Clutch Cam scales the whole block up; Agent Select stacks the two data strips above a larger handcam; Warmup Split puts the deck below the boxed gameplay.

